# infra/gateway/operator-env.example
#
# Operator-customization env file for personal / dedicated gateways.
#
# Copy this to /home/node/.openclaw/secrets/operator.env on the gateway's
# PVC (mode 600) and add additional credentials / integrations the
# platform doesn't manage. Survives every PVC reschedule. Helm + K8s
# don't see this file.
#
# Sourced by entrypoint.sh AFTER the platform K8s env block (so the
# operator can override their own gateway if absolutely necessary, though
# the intent is additive-only — don't override platform-critical things
# like OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN unless you know what you're doing). Sourced
# BEFORE envsubst on openclaw.template.json, so operator-defined values
# can populate the template on a first-boot gateway.
#
# See docs/architecture/GATEWAY-PLATFORM-SPEC.md
# §Operator-class customization surface for the design rationale.
#
# ── Editing on a running gateway's PVC ────────────────────────────────
# The gateway pod may be crash-looping, so use a debug pod that mounts
# the PVC (swap <ns> and <instance> for your gateway):
#
#   kubectl -n <ns> run pvc-edit --rm -it --restart=Never --image=alpine:3 \
#     --overrides='{"spec":{"containers":[{"name":"pvc-edit","image":"alpine:3","stdin":true,"tty":true,"command":["sh"],"securityContext":{"runAsUser":1000},"volumeMounts":[{"mountPath":"/data","name":"data"}]}],"volumes":[{"name":"data","persistentVolumeClaim":{"claimName":"octogee-gateway-<instance>-data"}}]}}' \
#     -- sh
#
# Then inside the shell:
#
#   mkdir -p /data/.openclaw/secrets
#   cat > /data/.openclaw/secrets/operator.env <<'EOF'
#   DISCORD_BENDER_TOKEN=...
#   EOF
#   chmod 600 /data/.openclaw/secrets/operator.env
#
# Then `kubectl rollout restart deployment/octogee-gateway-<instance>` to
# pick up the new env. Pod boots, entrypoint sources the file, openclaw
# resolves the ${VAR} references in openclaw.json.
#
# ── Examples ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Discord bot the operator drives from this gateway (referenced as
# ${DISCORD_BENDER_TOKEN} in openclaw.json):
# DISCORD_BENDER_TOKEN=...
#
# Personal Anthropic / OpenAI / xAI API keys the operator uses for
# their own coach work (above and beyond the BYO-subscription OAuth flow):
# PERSONAL_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
# PERSONAL_OPENAI_API_KEY=...
#
# Custom MCP server credential:
# CUSTOM_MCP_SERVER_TOKEN=...
